summary:
- topic: New Leadership
  text: The board officially welcomed new Superintendent Angela Atkinson Dena, who
    shared her initial observations and plans for her entry into the district. [Administration]
- topic: FY2026 Budget Update
  text: The Finance Director reported that due to a district-wide spending freeze,
    the FY26 budget is projected to land closer to a small surplus/deficit rather
    than the previously feared worst-case scenario, though the final outcome is still
    uncertain pending the audit. [Administration]
- topic: Spending Freeze Impact
  text: The spending freeze prompted a board discussion about its 'great cost' to
    teachers. A teacher representative (SPTA) later confirmed that essential supplies
    like paper and markers were unavailable, forcing teachers to use personal funds
    or share resources. [Board, Teachers]
- topic: Cell Phone Policy
  text: The board approved the second read of a new state-mandated cell phone policy
    (JICI) requiring phones to be off and away bell-to-bell. A lengthy discussion
    clarified that while the policy is set, the specific implementation procedures
    will be developed at the school level and reviewed by the board later. [Board,
    Administration]
- topic: Reconfiguration Workshop
  text: The meeting concluded with the first of several workshops on elementary school
    reconfiguration. The board and public participated in an activity to rank priorities,
    with board members later providing initial guidance emphasizing the need to address
    socioeconomic and demographic imbalances between schools. [Board, Citizens, Administration]
- topic: Public Comment
  text: Citizens expressed disappointment over the Kaler Elementary closure and urged
    better communication and funding for education. Teacher and parent representatives
    highlighted the real-world impact of the spending freeze on classrooms and the
    importance of neighborhood schools for working families. [Citizens, Teachers]
- topic: Key Approvals
  text: The board unanimously approved the consent agenda (including new hires and
    grants), the new cell phone policy, and a middle school field trip. [Board]
